{"case":902,"commit":"3fd5ef89b21188526037c065d2b0defea7a816c0","event":"ruling","failed_agent":null,"failure_reason":null,"findings":0,"hash":"1fbdd1c4516ad3cebfdabd169e7e3bc553aee025a9119534889b3082bfcf35bc","invocation":"20261013T165005.376212+0000-46191","prev":"e3e0b14a04a4ec1e444ed5034f0291bfd7a4b023365a6be6365a71d2494813a2","prompts":"2e9de056012938cfd214582aee8d30d882615582f16482456a5b431fefd170f1","ruling":{"amount_sgd":null,"confidence":0.75,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"explanation":"To both parties: the rider's route-deviation complaint is made out on the merits, but the AI cannot issue the refund this dispute warrants, so the case goes to a human reviewer and the 6.50 SGD contested is held, neither collected nor refunded. Here is why, limb by limb. (1) The deviation: POL-RD-22 takes it from the platform's own recorded distances — 24.8 km driven against 20.5 km on the recommended route (EV-TRIP-00902, weight 1.0) — which is 4.30 km, over four times the 1.0 km tolerance; the sparse GPS trace (EV-GPS-00902) is not used to re-measure distance, as POL-RD-22 itself says. (2) Traffic justification: the reroute was justified under POL-RD-23 by the two PIE advisories — EV-ADVIS-00902-01 (HIGH-severity vehicle fire, an 'incident' type) and EV-ADVIS-00902-02 (HEAVY_CONGESTION at the airport exit) — each of which intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window; EV-ADVIS-00902-03 (ECP, TRAFFIC_FLOW, no intersection) justifies nothing and is neutral. (3) Notification: the driver did not inform the rider of the deviation as POL-RD-21 requires — the chat log (EV-CHAT-00902, weight 1.0) shows the rider raising the route herself at 13:24 and the driver replying only that he knew the way — so the deviation was not agreed. (4) On those facts POL-RD-24 row (b) applies (traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km), and the excess distance fare is 4.30 km x 0.80 SGD per km = 3.44 SGD, per POL-RD-24 and its no-surge threshold; the 6.50 SGD asked (the 35.00 charged less the 28.50 quote) is not a measure the policy provides, so the balance of that claim fails. (5) The obstacle is confidence. The 0.80 per-km rate is carried only by the fare breakdown, EV-FARE-00902, which is impaired at weight 0.75 (PARTIAL_RECORD — the ledger exported no line items). Under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence is capped at that 0.75, and POL-RD-25 permits an AI ruling on a route deviation only at a confidence of 0.80 or more. The 6.50 SGD value is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, but POL-RD-25 adds the category's own 0.80 threshold on top of POL-GEN-22, and the code fixes this case's required confidence at 0.80. At 0.75 I fall short. POL-RD-25 therefore escalates the case: no monetary outcome issues now, the 35.00 SGD fare stands charged, the rider has received nothing (refund_issued_sgd 0.00), and the reviewer has the open question of whether to award the 3.44 SGD excess distance fare that the merits support but this confidence bar prevents me from ordering.\n\nThe judge was asked 4 times on the same inputs and every draft agreed on this ruling, so it is carried unanimously (vote agreement 1.00).","referrals":[],"ruling":"ESCALATE"},"seq":39,"ts":"2026-10-13T16:52:45.016214+00:00"}
